For each pair `(ℓ, Q)` below, `T(Q²)` kills `Σ p((ℓm+1)/24) q^{m/24}` modulo `ℓ`, so
`p((ℓQ³n+1)/24) ≡ 0 (mod ℓ)` for every `n` with `Q ∤ n` and `24 ∣ ℓQ³n + 1`.
Each instance has one kernel certificate (`wchk`) on `p(N) mod ℓ` and the hypothesis
`EtaHecke Q (ℓ−1) ℓ`. Pairs: (13,59) (13,73) (17,41) (17,89) (17,103) (19,101) (23,5) (23,19)
(23,37) (23,47) (23,67). Corollaries: Ono's `p(13·59⁴n + 111247) ≡ 0 (mod 13)` and Weaver's
`p(48037937n + 1122838) ≡ 0 (mod 17)`.
-/

